[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Queen's Pawn Game: Accelerated London System, 2...Nc6 and ...Bf5"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "fork,pin"]
[Themes "c4-break,b7-weakness"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2...Nc6 3.e3 Bf5"]
[Start "vs-d5-nc6 3.e3"]

3... Bf5 4. c4 { Strikes at d5 before Black's knight can go to b4. The bishop has left c8, so b7 is loose, and Qa4+ is ready if the knight jumps. }
4... e6
( 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 { Transposes to 4...e6 5.Nc3 Nf6. } )
( 4... Nb4 5. Qa4+ { Check, and the queen also attacks the knight on b4. Black cannot answer both. } 5... Bd7 ( 5... c6 6. Qxb4 ) 6. Qxb4 )
( 4... dxc4 5. Bxc4 e6 6. Nf3 )
( 4... e5 5. Bxe5 { Takes the pawn. If ...Nxe5, dxe5 and White is a pawn up. } )
5. Nc3 { A second attacker on d5. The knight also covers b5 and e4. }
5... Nf6
( 5... Nb4 6. Rc1 { The knight and the bishop on f5 both hit c2. The rook guards it, and a3 next sends the knight back. } 6... Bd6 7. Bxd6 Qxd6 8. a3 Nc6 )
( 5... Bb4 6. Rc1 )
( 5... dxc4 6. Bxc4 Bd6 7. Bg3 )
6. Nf3
6... Bd6
( 6... Bb4 7. Rc1 { If Black takes on c3, the rook takes back and White's pawns stay unbroken. } 7... O-O 8. a3 Bxc3+ 9. Rxc3 )
( 6... Be7 7. Rc1 )
( 6... Nb4 7. Rc1 )
( 6... dxc4 7. Bxc4 )
7. Bxd6 { Trades off the bishop that guards Black's dark squares, so the queen has to recapture. }
7... Qxd6 ( 7... cxd6 8. cxd5 Nxd5 9. Nxd5 exd5 10. Be2 ) 8. c5 { Gains space and hits the queen. Black's queen and knight lose the b4 and d6 squares. }
8... Qe7 9. Bb5 { Pins the knight on c6. Plan: castle, then Bxc6 and Ne5, or b4 and b5 to push on the queenside. } *
